      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel frustrated when solutions seem so simplistic compared to the massive systemic pressures you are facing. Your feeling that the system itself is rigged against upward mobility is a valid and heavy realization. While budgeting doesn't fix systemic inequality, sometimes connecting with groups focused on economic advocacy or financial reform can validate those feelings of injustice. Please remember that your worth is not determined by your bank account or your output as a worker.",
